course: dictionary
lesson: 12401
title: Curtly: few words, sharp feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Curtly is an adverb. It tells you how someone speaks or acts, and it comes from the adjective curt, which means short and rude.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «"Go away," the shopkeeper said curtly.» The words go away are short and unfriendly, and curtly tells you the shopkeeper spoke in that same cold way.
explain: Ask yourself: did the character use kind, friendly words, or only a few sharp ones? A curt answer uses very few words, and they sound annoyed or impatient.
explain: In stories you will meet curt characters, such as the Badger in The Wind in the Willows, who can be curt with Toad. In real life, a curt reply can make a friend feel unwelcome, so notice when it happens.
fact: Curtly means in a short, rude, unfriendly way, using very few words.
fact: Curtly is an adverb: it tells you how someone speaks or acts.
fact: Curt is the adjective, and curtly is the adverb that goes with it.
fact: Curtly often shows that someone is cold, annoyed or impatient.
fact: A curt reply can hurt feelings, even when it is only a few words long.
exercise: «"Go away," the shopkeeper said curtly.» What does curtly mean? | Very slowly, with a long story | *In a short, rude, unfriendly way | In a happy, friendly way | Quietly, so nobody can hear
exercise: «"Sit down," said the teacher curtly.» Find and copy the word that tells how the teacher spoke. | down | *curtly | teacher | sit
exercise: Why might a curt reply hurt someone's feelings? | It is sung very loudly | It is long and full of kind words | It makes the listener laugh | *It is short and rude, so it sounds unkind
test: «He nodded curtly and shut the door.» How did he nod? | Happily, with a big smile | *In a short, unfriendly way | Sadly, with tears in his eyes | Very slowly, one nod at a time
test: Which word means nearly the same as curtly? | Warmly | Gently | Slowly | *Rudely
exam: «"Leave now," the coach said curtly, and the team went quiet.» What does curtly tell us about the coach? | *The coach was cold and impatient | The coach was asleep | The coach was laughing and joking | The coach was lost
